<title>BELGIUM: GBL sees higher full-year 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>GBL sees higher full-year 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Groupe Bruxelles Lambert SA (GBL) said it expected full-year 1996 earnings to be higher than in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;1996 profit should be higher than in the previous year, independently of the capital gain which will be realised on the sale of Tractebel,&quot; the group said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The GBL group sold a 25 percent stake in utility holding company Tractebel SA last week.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
